------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE: WHAT THIS LICENSE COVERS IN THIS DISTRIBUTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------
In this distribution, the "Software" means everything here that the
copyright holder created:

   a. the tape files (.tzx), with everything they contain: the Sharp
      SM510 / SM5a emulator written for the ZX Spectrum, which runs the
      original LCD handheld games of every maker represented here
      (Nintendo, Tiger, Konami, Tronica, Elektronika, Nauchpribor and any
      others); the independently created greyscale screen graphics drawn
      for the Spectrum to depict each handheld; and the loaders;
   b. Munchy (MU-01), an original game, with its program, graphics and
      sounds;
   c. the script make_block2.py;
   d. the documentation; and
   e. the images and animated media in this distribution (the montage and
      per-maker contact-sheet GIFs).

Every tape shows an on-screen credit of two lines: a maker line reading
"<Maker>+ZXSpeccy forever!" — "Game&Watch+ZXSpeccy forever!" on the Nintendo
tapes and on Munchy, and "Tiger Elec+ZXSpeccy forever!", "Konami+ZXSpeccy
forever!", "Tronica+ZXSpeccy forever!", "Elektronika+ZXSpeccy forever!" or
"Nauchpribor+ZXSpeccy forever!" on the others — together with "SANYALnet
Labs". That "SANYALnet Labs" credit is the attribution Section 1(b)
requires, and it must stay visible in any copy or Derivative Work that has a
screen.

The original handheld game programs (ROMs) — from Nintendo, Tiger, Konami,
Tronica, Elektronika, Nauchpribor, or any other maker — are NOT included
here and are NOT covered by this license. Each user must supply their own.
The ROM tape that make_block2.py makes from a user's ROM holds only that
ROM; it is not part of the Software and must not be shared with it or as
part of it.


