THIRD-PARTY NOTICES
------------------------------------------------------------------------
The tapes contain no original program code (no ROMs) from any hardware
maker. Their screen graphics are new low-resolution drawings made for the
Spectrum to resemble the original handhelds' screens. This license grants no
rights in the original handhelds' designs, artwork, names, or the game,
film, television and character properties they depict, all of which remain
with their respective owners. The makers and properties below are named only
to identify which handhelds and games this software emulates; this project
is independent and is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by any
of them.

Hardware makers.
   - Nintendo. "Nintendo" and "Game & Watch" are trademarks of Nintendo Co.,
     Ltd.
   - Tiger Electronics. "Tiger Electronics" is a trademark of Hasbro, Inc.
   - Konami. "Konami" is a trademark of Konami Group Corporation.
   - Tronica. "Tronica" is a trademark of its respective owner.
   - Elektronika and Nauchpribor. "Elektronika" and "Nauchpribor" were
     brands of Soviet state manufacturers; their marks belong to their
     respective present owners.

Adapted properties. The Tiger and Konami handhelds depict arcade, film,
television, comic and sporting properties owned by or licensed to those
makers — among them Batman; the X-Men, Spider-Man and other Marvel and DC
characters; Altered Beast, Golden Axe, Space Harrier, Strider, Street
Fighter, Mortal Kombat, Double Dragon, Battletoads, Ninja Gaiden, Gauntlet,
Karnov, Castlevania and Mega Man; and film and television titles such as
Jurassic Park, Home Alone, Back to the Future, The Addams Family, The
Rocketeer, Wayne's World, Judge Dredd, GoldenEye and Independence Day. All
such names, titles, characters and logos are the trademarks and copyrights
of their respective owners.

Pac-Man. Munchy is an original maze game inspired by the classic maze-chase
genre. "PAC-MAN" is a trademark of Bandai Namco Entertainment Inc. Munchy is
not affiliated with or endorsed by Bandai Namco.

Sharp. "Sharp", "SM510" and "SM5a" name the 4-bit microcontrollers made by
Sharp Corporation, whose documented instruction behaviour this emulator
reproduces. The emulator is an independent implementation written for this
project; no Sharp program code or microcode is included. "Sharp" is a
trademark of Sharp Corporation.

MAME. make_block2.py reads ROM files in the form the MAME project uses. The
emulator was written for this project; for how the Sharp SM510 and SM5a
chips behave, it follows Sharp's data books as interpreted by MAME's SM510
emulation (BSD-3-Clause, copyright hap), which we gratefully acknowledge. No
MAME code is included.

ZX Spectrum. "ZX Spectrum" and "Sinclair" are trademarks of their respective
owners. No ZX Spectrum ROM is included; the tapes use the ROM of the user's
own computer or emulator.

All other product names, trademarks and registered trademarks named in this
distribution or its documentation are the property of their respective
owners and are used only for identification.
